WEBVTT

NOTE
Disc 1, Scene 14h: Battle of the Gardens — Collision and Combat
Duration: 37 seconds
Context: The two Gardens crash into each other in an unprecedented full-scale war between flying fortresses. This is the climactic confrontation between Balamb and Galbadia.
For blind and low-vision players using screen readers.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
The impact is catastrophic. Balamb Garden's white and blue structure collides with Galbadia Garden's red-brown mass. The collision generates a deafening crunch of metal scraping against metal. The entire landscape trembles. Both facilities lurch from the impact.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Walkways collapse under the force. Balconies crumble and fall away from both structures. Interior sections visible through fractured walls show chaos — furniture overturns, lights flicker and fail. The collision has torn open sections of both Gardens, revealing their internal layouts.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Hand-to-hand combat erupts where the two facilities lock together. SeeD cadets from Balamb clash with Galbadian soldiers in brutal melee combat. Combatants leap between the two facilities, using connecting bridges and damaged sections to traverse the gap. Weapons clash. Soldiers fall.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Galbadian paratroopers deploy from the red fortress. They descend via grappling lines and parachutes onto Balamb Garden's exterior surfaces. Gunfire erupts. SeeD members return fire. Explosions rock both structures as ammunition detonates in strategic locations.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Chaos defines the scene. Larger explosions bloom from both Gardens. The two massive facilities grind against each other, shifting and settling into a precarious locked position. Debris falls like rain into the ocean far below. This is a full-scale war — the most devastating military conflict in Balamb's history.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.000
The battle continues with no clear advantage for either side. Galbadia's numerical superiority faces off against Balamb's elite training. The two floating fortresses remain locked in combat, neither willing nor able to disengage. The fate of both Gardens now rests on the outcome of this catastrophic confrontation.